speechtext:
1.	What number of programmes (sketches) are broadcast by authority of the federal government over the English network of the CBC?
2.	What is the name of each programme or sketch and the name of the commentator?
3.	How many times weekly are these programmes broadcast?
Mr. LaFLECHE:
1 and 2. The national war finance committee, Department of Finance, has requested the services of the CBC's network to broadcast the following programmes:
"Highlights for Today";
"They Tell Me";
"Soldier's Wife".
At the request of the Department of National Defence (Air), the R.C.A.F. is broadcasting over the CBC a "Quiz Show".
No commentators are attached to the above programmes.
2.	(a) "Highlights for Today" is broadcast once weekly;
(b)	"They Tell Me" is broadcast five times weekly;
(c)	"Soldier's Wife" is broadcast five times weekly;
(d)	"Quiz Show" is broadcast once weekly.
